  "0": "Across all four datasets, keep real-item embeddings tied and normalized at the incumbent radius 0.75, but exempt the exclusive mask-token row from normalization, using its raw learned vector for input. A separately adaptable mask magnitude may improve masked-state conditioning without changing recommendation embeddings. Preserve frequency modulation, width, backbone, history, scoring, loss and optimizer; use the identical embedding definition in training and the predictor writer.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, replace chronological position IDs with reverse-distance IDs: the newest nonpadding token receives position 1, preceding tokens receive 2, 3, etc., and padding remains 0. Apply this consistently to masked training sequences and appended-mask inference. Recency anchoring may transfer better across the predominantly short, variable-length histories. Preserve history selection, final-mask readout, embeddings, backbone, scoring, loss and optimizer; update the predictor writer consistently.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, scale each Transformer feed-forward residual contribution by 0.8 while leaving attention residuals unchanged. The 0.5 trial's small regression motivates testing gentler attenuation that may retain useful nonlinear context transformations while limiting their distortion. Preserve GELU, block count, widths, normalization, bidirectional attention, embeddings, sequence policy, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Mirror the residual formula in the predictor writer.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, add label smoothing of 0.02 to the existing full-vocabulary masked-item cross-entropy, retaining temperature 0.8 and uniform weighting over masked targets. Mild smoothing may reduce overconfident item discrimination without the strong positional bias introduced by the regressed final-target weighting trial. Preserve masked-target sampling, embeddings, topology, scoring, readout, optimizer, scheduler and batch/epoch settings. Train and load exactly one checkpoint per category."
